<article class="env-lemma" id="0EBW">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EBW">Lemma <span data-tag="0EBW">51.17.2</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. If $f_1, \ldots , f_{r - 1}, f_ rg_ r$ are independent, then $f_1, \ldots , f_ r$ are independent. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Say $\sum a_ if_ i = 0$. Then $\sum a_ ig_ rf_ i = 0$. Hence $a_ r \in (f_1, \ldots , f_{r - 1}, f_ rg_ r)$. Write $a_ r = \sum _{i < r} b_ i f_ i + b f_ rg_ r$. Then $0 = \sum _{i < r} (a_ i + b_ if_ r)f_ i + bf_ r^2g_ r$. Thus $a_ i + b_ i f_ r \in (f_1, \ldots , f_{r - 1}, f_ rg_ r)$ which implies $a_ i \in (f_1, \ldots , f_ r)$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>